        "html": "<div class=\"lesson-content\">\n  <p class=\"lesson-intro\">The course tests understanding and hands-on ability, not the recital of theory — the final grade is made up of module quizzes, lab work, and a final project.</p>\n\n  <section class=\"lesson-section\">\n    <h2>Grading system</h2>\n    <p>We test understanding and hands-on ability, not recitation.</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"lesson-section\">\n    <h2>Final grade</h2>\n    <div class=\"lesson-table-scroll\">\n      <table>\n        <tr><th>Component</th><th>What it assesses</th><th>Weight</th></tr>\n        <tr><td>Module quizzes</td><td>Grasp of theory</td><td>30%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Lab work</td><td>Practice (commands, simulator)</td><td>45%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Final project</td><td>Building and troubleshooting a small network</td><td>25%</td></tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"lesson-section\">\n    <h2>Grading scale</h2>\n    <div class=\"lesson-table-scroll\">\n      <table>\n        <tr><th>Score</th><th>Level</th><th>What it means</th></tr>\n        <tr><td>90-100</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Builds and fixes a network independently, explains \"why\"</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>75-89</td><td>Good</td><td>Confident when working from an example, minor gaps</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>60-74</td><td>Satisfactory</td><td>Basic understanding is there, needs support</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>&lt;60</td><td>Fail</td><td>Needs to repeat the module</td></tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"lesson-section\">\n    <h2>Lab grading rubric</h2>\n    <div class=\"lesson-table-scroll\">\n      <table>\n        <tr><th>Criterion</th><th>What's checked</th><th>Max points</th></tr>\n        <tr><td>Functionality</td><td>The task is solved, the network works</td><td>40</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Correctness</td><td>Addressing and settings are correct</td><td>30</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Understanding</td><td>The student can explain their actions</td><td>20</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Presentation</td><td>Diagram/screenshots, tidiness</td><td>10</td></tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"lesson-section\">\n    <h2>Final project (modules 8-9)</h2>\n    <p>Build a network in Packet Tracer made up of two subnets connected by a router, with several workstations and a nominal \"outside\" connection. Configure addressing, get connectivity working between the subnets (<code>ping</code>), then find and fix one deliberately introduced fault. Report: diagram, configuration, how you tested it, what you fixed and why.</p>\n  </section>\n</div>\n"
